    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0504" n="1968" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg1968"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">689.90D/4–2151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Pakistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Karachi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-04-25T20:00:00+05:30">April 25, 1951—8
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1000. In two conversations today with Ikramullah and one with Dr. Mahmud Husain,
                    Min of States and Frontier Regions who is acting for Prime Minister, it was
                    agreed that text of GOP’s reply to our approach
                    as contained in Deptel 676, Apr 23 shld be
                    telegraphed to Prime Minister now in Peshwar this week. Mahmud Husain is
                    recommending to Prime Minister acceptance of textual language. As soon as reply
                    has been recd Ikramullah promises to inform me immed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
